A dispute between I'm A Celebrity&#x2026; Get Me Out Of Here! campmates AJ Odudu and Mariella Frostrup has sparked nearly 900 viewer complaints.

On Sunday evening, ITV broadcast footage of tensions between Big Brother host Odudu and broadcaster Frostrup over camp cooking duties (see below).

During one exchange, Frostrup accused Odudu of being &#x201C;aggressive&#x201D; and creating a &#x201C;drama out of a crisis.&#x201D; Odudu implored Frostrup not to &#x201C;use those words towards me,&#x201D; adding: &#x201C;&#x2018;Dramatic&#x2019; and &#x2018;aggressive&#x2019; are very harsh words.&#x201D; Related Stories News 'I'm A Celebrity's AJ Odudu Gets Support From 'BBUK' Co-Host Will Best & More Stars Amid Microaggressions On ITV Reality Series News ITV Issues Statement Amid Outcry Over AJ Odudu Experiencing "Microaggressions" On 'I'm A Celebrity... Get Me Out Of Here!'

Ofcom , the UK media regulator, revealed on Wednesday that it had received 887 complaints about the episode. An Ofcom spokesperson said: "We are assessing the complaints against our rules, but are yet to decide whether or not to investigate." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Odudu&#x2019;s experience prompted an outcry on social media. On Instagram, Strictly Come Dancing judge Motsi Mabuse wrote: &#x201C;I wish there were better ways to protect ourselves from microaggressions and the cumulative emotional toll they take.

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s a weight that many will never fully understand, and sadly, some won&#x2019;t even try. The exhaustion comes not only from experiencing it, but also from constantly having to explain why it hurts.&#x201D;

Presenter Clara Amfo said: &#x201C;Calling a Black woman &#x2018;aggressive&#x2019; when she is being anything but is a classic microaggression. Mariella&#x2019;s tears, doubling down and then doing &#x2019;sorry if,&#x2019; woefully predictable. This is deeply uncomfortable.&#x201D;

Producers spoke to Frostrup and Odudu after the incident, discussing what was said and why it might make someone uncomfortable.

In a statement, an ITV spokesperson said: &#x201C;The production monitors everyone in camp 24/7 and if at any time we feel someone has overstepped the line by using inappropriate language or displaying unacceptable behaviour, we would take steps to intervene and speak to everyone involved.

&#x201C;The duty of care for our contestants is of the utmost importance to us. We take the welfare of the celebrities very seriously and have measures in place to ensure they are supported at every stage of the process: before, during and after filming.&#x201D;

EXCLUSIVE: Scott Adkins and team behind Diablo are set to serve up some Brutal Justice . We&#x2019;ve got the first pics from the movie, which will be released next year. Adkins also told Deadline about a new film he has written and dished the latest on the prospect of more from the Undisputed franchise.

Diablo hit the number one spot on Paramount+&#x2019;s global movie charts earlier this year, having launched on the streamer in select international territories. It is on Tubi in the U.S. British martial artist and actor Adkins says they wanted to get the Diablo gang back together, which paved the way for Brutal Justice . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Well Go USA Acquires Nazi Revenge Film 'Vindicta' -- AFM Casting Isla Fisher & Blake Ritson Join Al Pacino In John Paul Getty III Kidnapping Pic 'Captivated'

&#x201C; Diablo had Marko (Zaror) co-starring and it was the first time I had worked with the director Ernesto D&#xED;az Espinosa who did a fantastic job; Craig (Baumgarten) produced it and it was a great experience,&#x201D; Adkins said. &#x201C;We shot it in Colombia and it has done really well. So, the idea was to do another film with Marko, Craig and with Ernesto as the director.&#x201D; Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Adkins added the Brutal Justice team shared a love of the same films: &#x201C;We&#x2019;re inspired by the same movies, and we all see things the same way and are heavily into the martial arts. The director wrote the script for [ Brutal Justice ], which was like Dirty Harry meets Death Wish , very 70s-inspired, and I'm the dirty cop, and Marko's character is the vigilante.&#x201D;

The Daro Film Distribution and Vault Entertainment-produced film follows a grief-stricken detective (Adkins) hunting a masked vigilante (Zaror). After discovering they&#x2019;re both targeting the same criminal empire and want to bring down the pharmaceutical kingpin who was responsible for their families&#x2019; deaths, the two join forces and set out seeking vengeance.

The film is in post production. Monaco-based Daro Film Distribution is handling worldwide sales and was at both MIPCOM and AFM with Brutal Justice . North America rights are with Vault Entertainment and the domestic distributor will be Samuel Goldwyn. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Adkins and Zaror, meanwhile, have previously appeared together in John Wick: Chapter 4 as well as Undisputed III: Redemption .

Adkins&#x2019; directorial debut is the upcoming action pic Brawler , which he also starred in, alongside Lewis Tan ( Mortal Kombat ). &#x201C;I always knew I'd do it; I waited until I was 50 and I don't know why it took me so long,&#x201D; Adkins said about moving into directing. He is also writing and shares details on an early-stage project called Last Fight .

&#x201C;I really like being creatively involved and have a lot of script ideas and things that I'm writing with other writers. [ Last Fight ] would sort of be my Kickboxer. We want to have that '90s vibe where it's fun and it's engaging and there are great martial arts action scenes. It's all about the martial arts, but also there's an emotional through-line that hopefully will be touching and grab the audience.&#x201D;

Adkins was, meanwhile, cool on the prospect of doing more in the Undisputed franchise, with the rights situation seemingly complicated. &#x201C;It doesn't look like it,&#x201D; the action star said when asked about the prospects of making a fifth picture. &#x201C;It doesn't seem like we can &#x2013; the rights are elsewhere &#x2013; [so,] unless the rights become available.&#x201D;

There was also talk of an Undisputed TV series. Adkins noted the challenges in taking the film mythology over to a series. &#x201C;I think it's hard to go from the movies &#x2026; does a TV series have those in its history, or do we start afresh? I wouldn't want to start fresh, but maybe you could do a TV show and you don't discuss the other movies, but they are there in the background &#x2026; but it gets complicated.&#x201D;
